      "problem": "A $5$-gallon jug of water costs $\\[math] 7.60.$ What is the price per quart?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert from gallons to quarts. There are $4$ quarts in each gallon, so we multiply the number of gallons by $4\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n5 \\times 4 = 20\n$$\n\nSo $5$ gallons is the same as $20$ quarts. Now, to find the price per quart, we divide the total price by $20\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n7.60 \\div 20 = 0.38\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water costs $\\[math] 0.38$ per quart.",
